WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.360
We have one of those big if true type of announcements
yesterday, President Joe Biden announced that

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:11.860
there will be enough vaccine supply for every
adult in the United States to get a coronavirus

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.790
vaccine by the end of May.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:20.130
Now, there will be enough supply and we will
have the resources to inject every dose or

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.900
two different things.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.030
But we'll talk about that.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:26.590
Let's look at the announcement from Joe Biden
made yesterday afternoon.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:33.250
Means we're now on track to have enough vaccine
supply for every adult in America by the end

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.250
of May.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.990
Let me say that again.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:44.400
When we came into office, the prior administration
had contracted for not nearly enough vaccine

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.840
to cover adults in America.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.350
We rectified that about three weeks ago.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:55.780
We were able to say that we'll have enough
vaccine supply for adults by the end of July.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:01.710
I'm pleased to announce today, as a consequence
of the stepped up process that I've ordered

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:06.830
and just outlined, this country will have
enough vaccine supply a say again for every

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:13.100
adult in America by the end of May, by the
end of May.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.640
That's progress.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.350
Important progress, but it's not enough to
have the vaccine supply.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:23.520
We need vaccinators, people to put the shots
in people's arms.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.760
So what exactly does this mean?

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.330
There will be enough vaccine doses for every
adult to get vaccinated.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.549
Is this possible?

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:33.570
Is it an overpromise?

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.420
There's a number of different considerations
here.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.720
And let's just kind of think it through, apply
the sniff test to it.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.240
First of all, remember that right now every
American is mostly every adult.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:51.520
Two of the vaccines are for 18 plus currently
authorized for 18 years of age and older individuals.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.890
The other is for 16 plus.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:02:01.369
So roughly when we say every American right
now, we mean every eligible American, which

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:05.299
is somewhere between 260 and 266.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:12.310
Let's call it 265 million people if we start
with those eligible age wise for the vaccine.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.970
So we're starting with 265.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:21.170
Then we look at as of today, March 3rd, what
is the number of people who are vaccinated?

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.530
In other words, we start with the 265.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:26.069
How many are all set and we can remove from
that?

00:02:26.069 --> 00:02:28.660
Well, 26 million people got both doses.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:36.370
So that drops us from 265 to 239 million eligible
Americans left to vaccinate.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:44.010
Of the 239 million that are left, an additional
25 and a half, 26 million have one dose from

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.819
the vaccines that need two doses.

00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:51.660
So we need to get those 26 million people
to 100 percent vaccination.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.660
We need another 26 million doses.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:03:00.890
So then we will have two hundred and thirteen
million people left to vaccinate in the remainder

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:08.450
of March, April and May, 213 million people
in what is roughly 89 days.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:13.540
That's a big stretch, but there is more considerations
here.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:21.340
Joe Biden is saying not that we will vaccinate
every eligible American by the end of May.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.019
He's saying we will have enough vaccines by
the end of May and it could take time from

00:03:26.019 --> 00:03:29.730
vaccine availability to actual injection.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.720
So that's one aspect of this.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:38.069
We also have to probably take off the top
that right now about 25 percent of adults

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:39.519
don't want the vaccine.

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.519
That's the latest number.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:42.160
It's been declining over time.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.870
More and more people want the vaccine over
time.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.920
But in reality, it's not really two hundred
and thirteen million people left to vaccinate.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.050
It's more like one hundred ninety eight million
when you account for those who as of right

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.159
now say that they don't want it.

00:03:56.159 --> 00:04:01.700
So the question becomes, will there be doses
for one hundred and ninety eight million people

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:07.540
to be vaccinated by the end of May, even if
it takes them a little longer to get vaccinated?

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:08.650
In theory, yes.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:11.560
It's not crazy to think that that's a number
that's going to be available.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:17.470
Moderna and Fizer continue to say they will
deliver enough together to cover 200 million

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.949
Americans by the end of May.

00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:23.389
That would be 400 million doses, but that
includes December, January, February.

00:04:23.389 --> 00:04:25.419
It includes what they've already done.

00:04:25.419 --> 00:04:30.500
And then Johnson and Johnson, the recently
approved third vaccine, which is a one dose

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.500
vaccine.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.310
They had contracted to deliver 87 million
vaccines by the end of May.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.189
Remember, with being one dose.

00:04:37.189 --> 00:04:40.520
Eighty seven million vaccines is enough for
87 million people.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.259
But it looks like JNJ is going to fall short.

00:04:43.259 --> 00:04:45.330
But there are some breathing room.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:50.801
Even if Johnson and Johnson does only a part
of the 87 million they contracted to do, it's

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:56.869
quite plausible that you will have enough
vaccines for every eligible American who wants

00:04:56.869 --> 00:04:59.369
a vaccine by the end of May.

00:04:59.369 --> 00:05:05.560
As I said earlier this week, every indication,
if you look at both what the Biden administration

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.089
is claiming and what the pharmaceutical companies
are claiming, every indication is that the

00:05:10.089 --> 00:05:16.580
challenge as we get into April and certainly
it may even start to be a challenge in March,

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:22.909
certainly by the end of April and definitively
by May, the challenge will be, do we have

00:05:22.909 --> 00:05:25.620
enough infrastructure to put the vaccines
into arms?

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:31.169
Because the amount of new doses we're going
to have in the next 80 days, even in the next

00:05:31.169 --> 00:05:36.149
40 days, is well beyond what we currently
are able to inject.

00:05:36.149 --> 00:05:39.460
We're going to need more vaccination sites
which are being launched.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:42.629
We're going to need more vaccinators who are
being hired.

00:05:42.629 --> 00:05:48.169
And we may be needing to run some of these
larger vaccination sites 24/7 to make this

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:49.169
happen.

00:05:49.169 --> 00:05:52.469
Having enough vaccines by May 31st is great.

00:05:52.469 --> 00:05:57.319
If you can't actually inject them for four
months, then it's sort of like, well, it's

00:05:57.319 --> 00:05:58.490
actually going to be four more months.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:03.229
Now, one important thing to know, and this
may increase the number of people that want

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.590
the vaccine.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:10.779
The CDC is expected to announce tomorrow,
Thursday, March 4th, that it's OK.

00:06:10.779 --> 00:06:17.469
They're going to give a go ahead for vaccinated
people to gather indoors in small groups without

00:06:17.469 --> 00:06:18.899
masks.

00:06:18.899 --> 00:06:23.639
This may encourage more people to want the
vaccine and it may lower the vaccine hesitancy.

00:06:23.639 --> 00:06:26.740
Remember, at one point sixty percent didn't
want the vaccine.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.770
That was down to 50, 40, 33.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:29.839
Now it's down to about 25.

00:06:29.839 --> 00:06:36.490
The CDC saying, hey, we've determined these
vaccines are effective enough that vaccinated

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:42.059
people, groups of exclusively vaccinated people,
small groups indoors without masks are OK.

00:06:42.059 --> 00:06:44.319
That will likely encourage more people to
say, I want the vaccine.

00:06:44.319 --> 00:06:50.199
Now, at the same time, the counter would be,
if you care what the CDC says, you probably

00:06:50.199 --> 00:06:51.300
already want the vaccine.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.500
You're already in the group of people that
want it.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.649
So maybe it won't make that big of a difference.

00:06:55.649 --> 00:07:01.679
I don't know if the CDC is going to convince
too many anti vaccines that at this late stage

00:07:01.679 --> 00:07:03.099
still don't want the vaccine.

00:07:03.099 --> 00:07:09.919
But it's something people who have been fully
vaccinated against covid-19 will be cleared

00:07:09.919 --> 00:07:12.810
to gather in small groups without masks.

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:19.020
Dr. Anthony Fauci said yesterday, quote, I
used the example of a doctor coming in from

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:23.839
out of town who is doubly vaccinated and a
husband and wife will be vaccinated and maybe

00:07:23.839 --> 00:07:30.629
a next door neighbor who, you know, are vaccinated
small gatherings in the home of people.

00:07:30.629 --> 00:07:36.349
I think you can clearly feel that the relative
risk is so low that you would not have to

00:07:36.349 --> 00:07:41.460
wear a mask that you could have a good social
gathering within the home.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.460
That is very good news.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:45.569
That is very optimistic news, and I find it
completely reasonable.

00:07:45.569 --> 00:07:54.529
Now, it goes without saying that if this new
vaccine timeline is accurate, we are again,

00:07:54.529 --> 00:07:58.439
I want to be realistically optimistic based
on what we're being told.

00:07:58.439 --> 00:08:03.110
We are looking at a potentially very good
summer, all else being equal, assuming we

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:07.379
don't have significant variant escape from
the vaccines and all of the things that we're

00:08:07.379 --> 00:08:12.419
watching, we're potentially looking at a pretty
solid summer and we will continue to cover

00:08:12.419 --> 00:09:59.350
it.

